# Copy to `.env.local` and edit. Every variable is optional; the defaults are
# the ones that make the template work against a local Passport.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Act one — connect
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The exact origin of the Passport app. Messages are posted to this origin and
# nothing else, and inbound messages from any other origin are dropped.
# Must be a DIFFERENT origin from this app.
# VITE_PASSPORT_ORIGIN=http://localhost:5175

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Act three — the optional payment (off by default)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Set to exactly `1` to arm the transaction request bridge. With it unset the
# transaction code never runs and the interface says so.
#
# Arming it here is only half of it: the payment also needs a full local
# Passport whose on-device wallet really holds NIGHT (faucet, or the Passport
# repository's fund-localnet.mjs on a localnet) AND has DUST registered via its
# "Register DUST" control — otherwise the approval sheet refuses with the
# wallet's own `insufficient-funds`, which is the designed behaviour. See
# "Honest caveats" in the README.
# VITE_DEMO_PAYMENT=1

# The unshielded address (`mn_addr…`) the payment would go to, on the same
# network as the connected Passport wallet. Act three stays off without it.
# VITE_DEMO_PAYMENT_ADDRESS=mn_addr_preview1…

# Amount in ATOMIC NIGHT units. 1 NIGHT = 1 000 000, so 100000 = 0.1 NIGHT.
# VITE_DEMO_PAYMENT_AMOUNT=100000

# Explorer link template for the transaction hash — {hash} is replaced with
# the 32-byte ledger transaction hash Passport reports. Set it to your
# network's explorer, or to an empty value to show the bare hash rather than
# a link that 404s.
# VITE_EXPLORER_TX_URL=https://explorer.1am.xyz/tx/{hash}?network=preview
